\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces  Climate-state and precession-phase fitted event rates without event-process controls. Fitted binned Poisson event rates from the LR04+\(\ce {CO2}\) model and the LR04+\(\ce {CO2}\)+precession-phase model are shown for (a) strong and (b) weak monsoon starts. Vertical lines mark observed event bins. This visualization omits same-type event history and sampling-resolution controls, so it is not the main reference model; it is included to show the slower climate-state rate modulation and the superposed precession-phase structure more clearly. Text boxes report likelihood-ratio tests for adding the two precession-phase terms to the LR04+\(\ce {CO2}\) model. LR04, \(\ce {CO2}\), and precession phase are from \citet  {lisiecki2005pliocene}, \citet  {bereiter2015revision}, and \citet  {laskar2004long}, respectively. }}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:climate_phase_hazards_no_event_baseline}{{S3}{7}{}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S4}{\ignorespaces  Extended-baseline predictor correlations. Correlations among predictors in the extended baseline, defined as the full predictive model used as the reference for additional-forcing sensitivity tests. The matrix includes same-type event history, Cheng composite sampling resolution~\citep  {cheng2016asian}, $-$LR04~\citep  {lisiecki2005pliocene}, \(\ce {CO2}\)~\citep  {bereiter2015revision}, and the sine and cosine terms used to represent precession phase~\citep  {laskar2004long}. LR04 is sign-inverted only for display, so its correlation with \(\ce {CO2}\) is positive; the fitted models use the original LR04 orientation. The strong correlation between $-{}$LR04 and \(\ce {CO2}\) is consistent with treating them as partly overlapping indicators of slow glacial background state. Precession-phase terms are only weakly correlated with the event-process and background-state controls. }}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:extended_baseline_correlation}{{S4}{8}{}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S5}{\ignorespaces  Additional-forcing sensitivity. Sensitivity of predictive-information models to additional forcings. (a,b) \(\Delta \)AICc for strong and weak monsoon starts, measured relative to the extended baseline, i.e., the full predictive model before adding extra forcings. (c,d) Nested likelihood-ratio tests for the extra forcings. Bars show \(-\log _{10}(p)\), and the dashed line marks \(p=0.05\); bars to the left of this line are not significant. The three blocks test, from top to bottom, adding individual forcings to the extended baseline, adding all extra forcings jointly, and the unique contribution of each forcing within the full extended model. }}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sensitivity_aicc_lrt}{{S5}{9}{}{figure.5}{}}
